<section aria-labelledby="size-h">
  <h2 id="size-h" class="type-h2">Size</h2>
  <p>The card sits on the raised surface with a 1px border. The padding is 16px on mobile and 24px from 768px up. The title uses the H3 style and the text uses the Body style, so both step down on mobile. In a row of cards, every card is the same height and the buttons line up at the bottom.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using the link card</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Make the card the link, and name the link with the card title (<code>aria-labelledby</code> pointing at the title).</li>
      <li>Hide the button from screen readers (<code>aria-hidden="true"</code>). It is a look, not a control.</li>
      <li>Keep the text to one short line about the page.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Put a real button or another link inside the card. A link cannot hold another control.</li>
      <li>Point one card at more than one page.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="html-h">
  <h2 id="html-h" class="type-h2">The HTML</h2>
